# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Amber Community Dashboard — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored — credentials never reach the repo) and fill
# in what you have. Every integration degrades on its own: with nothing set the
# dashboard runs on demo data and labels it as such, so you can wire the
# sources up one at a time and a partial setup never breaks the rest.
#
# All three sources feed Community #2 only (see `integrations` in
# lib/groups.ts). Community #1 is manual-only and reads nothing from here.
#
# QUICK MAP — what goes where:
#   (1) Google service-account credentials
#         → GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON            (whole key file, one line)
#           — or the pair —
#         → GOOGLE_CLIENT_EMAIL + GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY
#   (2) Landing-page registrations sheet → GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID
#   (3) GA4 property                     → GA4_PROPERTY_ID
#   (4) Short.io (scholarship_teamB links)
#         → SHORTIO_API_KEY *and* SHORTIO_DOMAIN_ID (both required)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- (1) Google service account (shared by Sheets + GA4) --------------------
# One service account covers both Google sources. Create it in Google Cloud,
# enable the "Google Sheets API" and the "Google Analytics Data API", then:
#   • share the registrations sheet with the service-account email (Viewer)
#   • add the same email as a Viewer on the GA4 property
#
# EITHER paste the whole downloaded key file as one line...
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","client_email":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"}
#
# ...OR set the two fields separately (keep the \n escapes in the key):
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_EMAIL=dashboard@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMII...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# --- (2) Landing-page registrations sheet -----------------------------------
# The ID is the long string in the sheet's URL:
# https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS PART>/edit
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID=1AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz0123456789
#
# Optional; defaults to the first sheet's columns A:Z.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_RANGE=Registrations!A:Z
#
# Columns are matched by HEADER NAME, not position, and matching ignores case,
# spaces and punctuation ("Targeted country" == "targeted_country"). Column
# order and extra columns don't matter. Recognised headers:
#   timestamp   → Timestamp, Date, Submitted At, Submission Date,
#                 Created At, Date Time, Signup Date            (REQUIRED)
#   country     → Country, Targeted Country, Target Country, Destination,
#                 Destination Country, Country of Study, Study Country,
#                 Preferred Country, Country of Interest        (optional)
#   name        → Name, Full Name, Student Name, First Name, Your Name
#   email       → Email, Email Address, Mail, Email ID
#   university  → University, College, School, Targeted University
#   utmSource   → UTM Source, Source
#   utmMedium   → UTM Medium, Medium
#   utmCampaign → UTM Campaign, Campaign
#
# Timestamp is the only hard requirement — it places a row in a week. Extra
# columns the dashboard has no field for (Mobile number, Target city, Intake
# year, application stage, …) are ignored harmlessly.
#
# Sheet named a column something not listed? Add the alias to
# lib/integrations/sheet-columns.ts — never rename your sheet to suit the code.
# With no UTM columns present, every lead groups under "Other" in the
# leads-by-source breakdown; the Sheets status pill says so explicitly.

# --- (3) GA4 -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Property ID — digits only, from GA4 Admin → Property Settings. Uses the same
# service account as the sheet; there is no separate GA4 key.
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=123456789

# --- (4) Short.io ------------------------------------------------------------
# BOTH variables are required — the key alone is not enough:
#   API key:   Short.io dashboard → Integrations & API → API keys.
#   Domain ID: numeric ID of the domain holding your tracked links.
# The dashboard counts only links tagged with the community's tag from
# lib/groups.ts — currently `scholarship_teamB` for Community #2, the only
# community the Short.io data represents. The tag lives on the links in
# Short.io, not in this file.
# SHORTIO_API_KEY=sk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# SHORTIO_DOMAIN_ID=123456

# --- Persistence for manual weekly entries ---------------------------------
# Default: a JSON file at data/weekly-entries.json. No setup needed.
# To use Supabase instead, set both of these and run supabase/schema.sql.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# --- Tuning ----------------------------------------------------------------
# How long a pull is reused before the next page load re-pulls. Default 10 min.
# INTEGRATION_CACHE_TTL_MS=600000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERIFYING A CONNECTION (after restarting the server)
#
# Each source reports its own status independently:
#
#   • Header pills on Community #2 and Merged pages — one pill per source.
#     "Sheets · demo" flips to "Sheets" with an accent dot once live;
#     "· error" means credentials reached the code but the pull failed
#     (hover the pill for the exact error message).
#   • The demo-data banner lists only the sources still on demo data and
#     disappears entirely once all three are live.
#   • From a terminal:  curl http://localhost:3000/api/refresh
#     forces a fresh pull and returns JSON — per-source status + message,
#     and row counts (registrations / ga4Rows / shortLinks).
#
# The "Refresh data" button in the header re-pulls on demand; otherwise a pull
# is cached for INTEGRATION_CACHE_TTL_MS and refreshed on page load when stale.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
